---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ChapterBreak from "../components/ChapterBreak.astro";

// ─── copy provenance key ────────────────────────────────────────────
// LIFTED  = pulled verbatim or near-verbatim from ctpvisibility.com
// DRAFTED = written from Danny's positioning context (the substrate-
//           changed reframe + markup-gap two-doors) for Abbey to revise
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

const pillars = [
  { num: "I",   name: "Interpretation",  gloss: "What AI believes about your brand." }, // LIFTED
  { num: "II",  name: "Retrievability",  gloss: "How often, and where, you appear." }, // LIFTED
  { num: "III", name: "Authority",       gloss: "Whether models trust your expertise." }, // LIFTED
  { num: "IV",  name: "Defensibility",   gloss: "How protected you are from distortion." }, // LIFTED
];

const amazonUrl = "https://www.amazon.com/Super-Human-SMALL-Ways-While/dp/B0GX1F931T";
---

<Base
  title="CTP Visibility Advisors — Reputation built for an AI-mediated world"
  description="AI didn't invent brand visibility. The substrate changed; the discipline didn't. Strategic reputation work for an AI-mediated world."
>

  <!-- ─── §00 HERO  [LIFTED hero line + subhead] ────────────────── -->
  <section class="hero frame">
    <div class="preface">— Notes on reputation, in the AI era —</div>
    <h1>
      Building reputations <span class="accent">AI and humans</span> recognize instantly.
    </h1>
    <p class="subhead">
      Your brand is already being processed by AI. Make sure you get the reputation you've earned.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn" href="/check">See how AI sees your brand</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#doors">Ways to work together</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ChapterBreak />

  <!-- ─── §01 THE PREMISE  [DRAFTED — substrate-changed reframe] ── -->
  <section class="frame" id="premise">
    <div class="chapter"><span class="num">Chapter I</span> A premise.</div>
    <h2>None of this was invented in 2025.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Brand reputation, the discipline, is decades old. Getting interpreted
      accurately. Surfaced in the right rooms. Trusted by gatekeepers.
      Protected from competitors trying to rewrite your story. That craft
      existed long before language models had an opinion about you.
    </p>
    <p>
      What changed is the substrate. The rooms got bigger. The gatekeepers
      got faster. One of those gatekeepers is now a model that has read
      everything ever written about you in the time it takes to refill
      your coffee.
    </p>
    <p class="pullquote">
      The substrate changed. The discipline didn't.
    </p>
    <p>
      That's the lens behind the work here. Not a new playbook bolted on
      top of panic. The same craft you'd want anyway, applied to systems
      that now talk about you whether you like it or not.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      Section drafted from positioning. To be revised in the founder's voice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <ChapterBreak />

  <!-- ─── §02 FOUR PILLARS  [LIFTED — schema FAQ-friendly] ──────── -->
  <section class="frame" id="pillars">
    <div class="chapter"><span class="num">Chapter II</span> What's actually happening.</div>
    <h2>AI visibility, in four parts.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The work breaks down into four dimensions. Each one is measurable.
      Each one is fixable. None of them get fixed by writing more blog posts.
    </p>

    <dl class="pillars" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">
      {pillars.map((p) => (
        <div class="pillar" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
          <dt itemprop="name">
            <span class="num">{p.num}</span>
            {p.name}
          </dt>
          <dd itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
            <p itemprop="text">{p.gloss}</p>
          </dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <ChapterBreak />

  <!-- ─── §03 ABOUT  [LIFTED bio, DRAFTED arc framing] ──────────── -->
  <section class="frame" id="about">
    <div class="chapter"><span class="num">Chapter III</span> Behind the practice.</div>
    <h2>A note on the founder.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      CTP Visibility Advisors is led by Abby Lovett, who brings 25+ years
      of experience protecting and promoting world-class brands across
      Fortune 100 companies, bold disruptors, and franchise systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      Strategic marketing communications, reputation building, integrated
      brand solutions. She works with clients and colleagues who are
      like-minded, professionally generous, and operate with integrity —
      and she has a deep commitment to paying it forward.
    </p>

    <div class="arc">
      <div class="arc-item">
        <div class="role"><span class="num">i</span> Operator</div>
        <p>Two and a half decades inside the rooms where reputation is actually decided — Fortune 100, disruptors, franchise systems.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="arc-item">
        <div class="role"><span class="num">ii</span> Author</div>
        <p><em>Super Human</em> — a plain-spoken, research-backed roadmap for thriving at work amid the noise. Out 2026.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="arc-item">
        <div class="role"><span class="num">iii</span> Practice</div>
        <p>CTP Visibility Advisors. Audits, strategy, and ongoing monitoring for organizations that want to be interpreted accurately.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ChapterBreak />

  <!-- ─── §04 TWO DOORS  [DRAFTED — markup-gap positioning] ─────── -->
  <section id="doors">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="chapter"><span class="num">Chapter IV</span> Two ways in.</div>
      <h2>Two doors. The same craft.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Most engagements come through one of two paths. Both get the same
        care. Neither involves keyword stuffing, fly-by-night tools, or
        anything that would make you uncomfortable saying out loud.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="doors-split">

      <article class="door door--agencies">
        <div class="door-inner">
          <div class="who">For agencies & comms partners</div>
          <h3>White-label visibility audits and strategic build-outs.</h3>
          <p class="what">
            You already own the client relationship. We sit underneath,
            doing the specialized work that doesn't fit inside a retainer
            designed for press, social, or paid. You keep the front of the room.
          </p>
          <ul class="includes">
            <li>AI visibility audit, full four-pillar</li>
            <li>Strategic plan, scoped to the client's category</li>
            <li>Quarterly monitoring and competitor watch</li>
            <li>Co-branded or fully white-labeled deliverables</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#close">Start a partnership conversation</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="door door--brands">
        <div class="door-inner">
          <div class="who">For franchise systems & brand owners</div>
          <h3>Productized engagements, direct.</h3>
          <p class="what">
            For founders and franchise leaders who want the work done without
            a middle layer. Tiered packages with clear scope. Every paid
            engagement includes a copy of <em>Super Human</em>.
          </p>
          <ul class="includes">
            <li>Tier I — Visibility audit and 90-day plan</li>
            <li>Tier II — Audit, plan, and quarterly monitoring</li>
            <li>Tier III — Embedded advisory across a calendar year</li>
            <li>Custom — for franchise systems with multi-location footprints</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#close">Talk about your brand</a>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>

    <div class="frame">
      <p class="note">
        Tier names and scope drafted as placeholders. Final SKU language is the founder's call.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ChapterBreak />

  <!-- ─── §05 BOOK  [LIFTED title + premise, DRAFTED framing] ───── -->
  <section class="frame" id="book">
    <div class="chapter"><span class="num">Chapter V</span> The book.</div>
    <h2>Super Human.</h2>

    <div class="book-module">
      <a class="book-cover" href={amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Super Human by Abby Lovett — open on Amazon">
        <img
          src="https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51-PLdl8D9L._SY522_.jpg"
          alt="Super Human — book cover. Heart-with-cape mark on a navy field."
          loading="lazy"
          width="345"
          height="522"
        />
      </a>

      <div>
        <p class="lede">
          <em>Super Human: 8 "SMALL" ways to be super at what you do … and human while you do it.</em>
        </p>
        <p>
          A plain-spoken, research-backed roadmap for thriving at work amid
          all the noise. The same lens that grounds the client work. Every
          paid engagement ships with a copy.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn" href={amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read on Amazon</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ChapterBreak />

  <!-- ─── §06 CLOSE  [DRAFTED — gentle closing CTA] ─────────────── -->
  <section class="frame" id="close">
    <div class="chapter"><span class="num">Chapter VI</span> Let's talk.</div>
    <h2>Tell us what's actually happening with your brand.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The fastest way to start is a short note. Whether you're an agency
      partner or a brand owner. What's prompting the conversation. Where
      you'd like to be six months from now.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row" style="justify-content: flex-start;">
      <a class="btn" href="mailto:abby.lovett@ctpvisibility.com?subject=Visibility%20conversation">
        abby.lovett@ctpvisibility.com
      </a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/check">Or run the free check first</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
